Downsizing Criteria
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Max memory usage < 40% and Max CPU usage < 40%
Downsize both Memory and CPU

Downsize Memory
Max memory usage < 40% and Max CPU usage > 40%
Max memory usage > 40% and Max CPU usage < 40%
Max memory usage > 40% and Max CPU usage > 40%
Downsize CPU

No opportunity to downsize.

Notes

Don't change the version of the sizes which we are reducing
D series VM will be changed to next lower D series SKU
E series to its next lower E series VM SKU
F series to its next lower F series VM SKU.
D series VM will be changed to F series VM SKU with same cores
E series will be be changed to D series will same cores
F series doesn't have opportunity to downsize.
D series will be changed to E series VM SKU with next lower core count
F series will be changed to D series with lower core count
E series doesn't have opportunity to downsize.

Example

Lets consider we have a general purpose VM with SKU D4as_v5 with specifications of 4 vCPU and 16GB of memory.
Post analysis of New Relic report of last 3 months for the server, we find that the Maximum utilization is of CPU is 30% and memory is 35%.
We will consider it to get resized to D2as_v5 with specifications of 2 vCPU and 8GB of memory, because post resize the utilization will be CPU at 60% and memory is 70% which will be well below the threshold values.
